From 1e07a688a3bf91eb3f0146d60585fe554e0a497e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:54:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Round 6: Run one batch worker on the calling thread

Spawn one scoped thread fewer than the requested worker count (bounded
by the number of index ranges) and run the same range-claiming loop on
the calling thread, which previously only waited for the scope. Items
still go to per-index slots, so record order and content do not depend
on the thread that evaluated them.

Workload: parallel (96 full records, 62 steps each, four workers on a
2-vCPU host).
Before median: 0.2775 ms. After median: 0.2169 ms. Speedup: 1.28x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
